window.KOW_HELP_HTML_EN = '<div class="notice"><b>Recommended workflow:</b> work through Officer → Stars → Development → XP → Planner, then use <b>Save Progress</b>. Use <b>Backup & Restore</b> in Settings before major changes or when you want a portable copy of locally saved app data.</div>\n\n      <h3>1. Officer</h3>\n      <p>Use <b>Search</b>, <b>Season</b> and <b>Officer Type / Role</b> filters to narrow the Officer list. Select the Officer you want to calculate. A matching portrait is displayed automatically when its file is available in the <b>officer-portraits</b> folder.</p>\n      <p>The selected Officer determines the cost of an Officer Badge in <b>Officer Readiness Vouchers (ORV)</b> and the cost of an Exclusive Star in <b>Star Readiness Vouchers (SRV)</b>.</p>\n      <p>The <b>Officer Upgrade Summary</b> shows the remaining Officer Badges, Officer Stars and Officer XP for the currently selected Officer.</p>\n      <p><b>Original Officers:</b> Officer Readiness Vouchers (ORV) and Star Readiness Vouchers (SRV) cannot be used for Original Officers.</p>\n\n      <h3>2. Stars</h3>\n      <p>Set the Officer\'s current and target Star level. Enter Legendary Star I, II and III held and <b>Star Readiness Vouchers (SRV)</b> held. The app calculates Officer Star value held, Exclusive Stars obtainable from SRV and the remaining Star requirement.</p>\n\n      <h3>3. Development</h3>\n      <p>Enter unlock status, completed Skill Points and Training Level. Then enter Officer Badges Held, <b>Universal Legendary Badges Held</b>, <b>Legendary Officer Badge Selection Chests Held</b> and <b>Officer Readiness Vouchers (ORV) Held</b>.</p>\n      <p>Each <b>Universal Legendary Badge</b> is worth <b>1 Officer Badge</b> for a Legendary Officer.</p>\n      <p>Each <b>Legendary Officer Badge Selection Chest</b> can be used as <b>either</b> 1 Universal Legendary Badge <b>or</b> converted to the latest-Season Officer Readiness Voucher (ORV) value. A chest cannot count as both. With the current S7 database the benchmark is <b>600 ORV per chest</b>.</p>\n\n      <h3>4. XP</h3>\n      <p>Enter current and target Officer Level, then enter the number of Officer XP Books held in each denomination. The app calculates XP held, XP required and the remaining shortfall.</p>\n\n      <h3>5. Planner & Resource Optimiser</h3>\n      <p>Use Planner after entering Stars, Development and XP. Select a goal such as Max Officer, Next Star, Reach 5★, Max Skills or Max Training to see requirements, resources held and shortfalls.</p>\n      <p>The <b>Resource Optimiser</b> lets you select a second Officer in <b>Compare with Officer</b>. It compares the Officer Readiness Voucher (ORV) cost per Officer Badge for the two Officers.</p>\n      <p><b>How to interpret the recommendation:</b> where both Officers can use ORV, the optimiser recommends favouring ORV on the Officer with the <b>lower ORV cost per badge</b> and favouring shared <b>Universal Legendary Badges / Legendary Officer Badge Selection Chests</b> on the Officer with the <b>higher ORV cost per badge</b>. This protects the more expensive Officer from unnecessary ORV spending.</p>\n      <p>The optimiser is <b>preview only</b>. It does not automatically spend, allocate or change your saved resources.</p>\n\n      <h3>5a. Multi-Officer Upgrade Planner</h3>\n      <p>The Multi-Officer Planner lets you create a priority list of several Officers, set the Officer Badges still needed for each, and preview how shared ORV, Universal Legendary Badges and Legendary Officer Badge Selection Chests could cover the plan.</p>\n      <p>Use <b>Use current held resources</b> to copy the resources currently entered in Development. Plans are preview-only and do not spend or alter the normal calculator data. Named plans can be saved locally in the browser and loaded again later.</p>\n\n      <h3>6. Save Progress</h3>\n      <p>Use <b>Save Progress</b> after entering or changing calculator information. Progress is stored locally in the browser on the current device. Save Progress does not publish your personal data to other users.</p>\n\n      <h3>7. Database</h3>\n      <p>The Database Manager controls the Officer master list. Use it to add or edit Officers and export the database. <b>Export CSV</b> exports the Officer database; it is different from Save Progress and App Backup.</p>\n      <p>To publish new or edited Officers for everyone, update the published <b>officers.json</b> and <b>officers.csv</b> files in the GitHub repository.</p>\n\n      <h3>8. Settings, Backup & Restore</h3>\n      <p>Settings contains the app name, portrait and landscape backgrounds, update controls and <b>Backup & Restore</b>.</p>\n      <p><b>Export App Backup</b> creates a JSON backup of KoW Companion data stored locally by the browser. Keep this file somewhere safe. <b>Restore App Backup</b> loads a previously exported JSON backup and reloads the app.</p>\n      <p><b>Check for Updates</b> compares the installed version with the published version. <b>Refresh Latest Version</b> refreshes the KoW Companion application cache without intentionally deleting saved calculator progress.</p>\n\n      <h3>Terminology</h3>\n      <p><b>ORV</b> = Officer Readiness Voucher<br>\n      <b>SRV</b> = Star Readiness Voucher<br>\n      <b>Universal Legendary Badge</b> = 1 Officer Badge for a Legendary Officer<br>\n      <b>Exclusive Star</b> = 110 Officer Star value</p>';
